1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,300
My mum doesn't know CAD
or 3D printers.

2
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:06,700
She just talks to Mıstık.

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:10,300
Mum: Mıstık, can you print me
a little gift box for flowers?

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,400
Mıstık: Mum, I found two.
1) Flower box, about 2 h 16 min

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:15,600
2) Plant pot, about 4 h 34 min.
Which one?

6
00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:17,400
Mum: The first one, a white box.

7
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:20,800
Mıstık: Queued (#7).
It starts when the owner approves.

8
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,200
Mum: Lovely, print it please!

9
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:25,000
[Blocked: owner approval needed]

10
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:27,500
Owner: /home3d approve start 7
Started #7.

11
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:30,800
The rules are in code.
Only the owner starts. Anyone can stop.

12
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,300
A watcher checks the printer
every two minutes.

13
00:00:34,400 --> 00:00:36,800
No model calls, no tokens.

14
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:39,700
It writes only when something happens.

15
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:44,300
Mıstık: Mum, the flower box is done.
Pushed off: pick it up from the box.

16
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:46,800
[To the owner: layers, temps, photo]

17
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:51,600
When the bed cools, the printer
pushes the part off by itself.

18
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,600
We asked it to clear the plate
without a person.

19
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:59,000
It tried a push,
and the part got stuck at the front.

20
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:03,400
It found a tilted base
and printed its own upgrade.

21
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:05,800
The plugin makes this a rule:

22
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:09,800
when a human task repeats,
it proposes an upgrade.

23
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:13,800
No printer?
Try it with the simulator.

24
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,500
One command:
hermes home3d demo

25
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:24,500
Mıstık.
The home's 3D workshop.
